Hi [~accountid:6358f0a501c2ff842c182ef2] my research leads to the conclusion that the presented campaign will be recognized as a promotional lottery (loteria promocyjna) under the Polish Act on Hazard Games. As a consequence:

* to run the campaign, Bolt would need to apply for the permission (zezwolenie) of “Dyrektor Izby Administracji Skarbowej”;
* the fee for granting permission amounts to 10% of prize pool, not less than 50% of “the average monthly salary in the enterprise sector without payments of rewards from profit, in the second quarter of the previous year, announced in the announcement of the President of the Central Statistical Office in the Official Journal of the Central Statistical Office“ (which amounts to PLN 7540,36 gross);
* permission is granted within 2 months from issuing the request;
* if you decide to run the campaign without permission, the penalty amounts to 5 x fee for permission;
* apart from the penalty above, the head of the tax office may also impose a penalty of up to PLN 100,000 on persons acting as managers or members of the board of directors of an entity arranging a lottery without a permit.

Hope this helps, regards, Piotr

