Hi [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] - my thoughts on your Qs are below.

{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}
*DRIVERS*
{panel}

{quote}*_Is there any channel where we can ask questions from Engineers related to the data?_*{quote}

No specific channel. However:

* The main engineer Project Green eng/product POCs are Alex Sivkov, Nikita Lakeev (drivers) and Taras Sgibnev (riders), so they should be the starting point.
* The main Project Green channel for general Qs is [https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C07R84XBR45|https://bolt.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C07R84XBR45|smart-link] 

{quote}*_Price bids - can we confirm with engineers, including Evgenii, whether this data would be added to the order history?_*{quote}

Price bidding as a feature is being discussed on this SD ticket ([+LSS-48927+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-48927]). In the order history in the app (and invoices), only the final price will be visible to drivers and riders. However, the full bidding history will be available in Admin to Bolt employees.

{quote}*_List of substitutes - can we confirm with engineers where it would be stored in Admin? Ideally, we need to add this and export as part of the Driver Profile plugin in the export tool._*{quote}

Mid-order substitution as a feature is being discussed in this SD ticket ([+LSS-48925+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-48925]). I would address this question Alex Sivkov either in Slack or on that ticket.

{quote}*_Substitute drivers - what specific info will be provided about another driver? Did we consider it as part of DSAR? While it concerns the Driver A, for trusted contacts we ended up not providing this data as DSAR. Should we add this for driver substitutes?_*{quote}

I have asked the question of what data will be provided on [+LSS-48925+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-48925], and am waiting on a response. I imagine what will be displayed about Driver B is profile picture, name and contact information.

IMO, we should not provide profile picture and contact information about Driver B. However, providing names is low risk, and is something we could consider providing. 

{quote}*_Substitute drivers taking a trip - I would consider not providing this data in the export tool, eg we need to export only data of the Driver A to him and Driver B to him._*{quote}

Agreed. This is just something to be aware of. We need to understand how t5his will be integrated into Admin, so that we can efficiently extract the data about the right driver.

Currently, the plan is +_not_+ to show substitutions in order history. This is due to bandwidth on the Ops / Eng side, as they do not have time to integrate it for now. I would address any other Qs to Alex Sivkov and Nikita Lakeev.

{quote}*_Driver B status - it should be added to the Driver Profile data of the Driver B. While Driver B can acts as a normal driver, we may add to the Profile details that this driver is also a substitute of Driver A._*{quote}

Noted that a user’s status as a ‘Driver B’ (substitute) instead of a ‘Driver A’ (regular driver) will be dealt with under separate profile IDs. See details of the feature on [+LSS-48925+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-48925], in which I have summarised this. I have otherwise asked this question on the ticket 🙂 

{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}
*PASSENGERS*
{panel}

{quote}*_Principal vs agency - is this a part of DSAR for the passenger? Does it matter what model the driver leveraged for the trip? I would propose not to disclose this as it may require additional development to add to the passenger’s order history_*{quote}

I think it should be, yes. It should be included in order history in the same way that we could include the category of a particular trip.

IMO we should develop this functionality, as it is foreseeable that a passenger may ask (I want details of all the trips I have taken under the agency model only). We need an efficient way of extracting this.

{quote}*_History of bids - can we confirm with engineers, including Evgenii, whether this data would be added to the order history?_*{quote}

This data will not be visible in the order history in the app. However, I agree that we should include the passenger’s bids in their order history. I have not yet reached out to Evgenii on this - however, I have flagged on [+LSS-48927+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-48927] that we need to have a functionality for extracting this data from Admin.

