Hey [~accountid:632ac798b2e3c5ad0fa1dd3e] [~accountid:712020:e3eb0c19-de7a-462e-8c6b-0a0de42d2687] - I apologise for the delay on this. I am coming back with a summary of my recommendations, all in one place, so apologies for the long read - I want to make sure I am not missing anything 🙂 

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Summary - Privacy position*
{panel}

:green_circle: This feature can proceed, but the following conditions must be met:

* We are processing third-party personal data (name + phone number) of someone who is not a Bolt user.
* The legal basis for this processing is legitimate interest, with the user acting as an intermediary who provides the data for a functional purpose (ride).
* Data minimisation is ensured as the fields are optional, and only name and phone number are collected (no payment data or location history is stored against the non-user).
* The phone number is masked, where technically feasible, and the non-user can be contacted only for trip-related purposes.

----

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Disclaimer* 
{panel}

Yes, a privacy disclaimer is required at the point of entering a third-party’s details.

h5. Recommended copy:

{quote}_“By booking a ride for someone else, you confirm that you have their permission to share their name and phone number with Bolt for the purpose of arranging the ride. This information will be shared with the driver for this purpose only. For more on how we handle personal data, please see our_ +_Privacy Notice_+_.”_{quote}

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Is explicit opt-in (checkbox) needed?*
{panel}

Not required. The notice can be passive, so long as it is clearly presented and reasonably assumed the user acts with the other person's awareness/consent. This balances UX friction and privacy risk -similar to other platforms with booking-for-others flows (e.g., Uber, Deliveroo, airlines).

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
h4. *Data storage, deletion and user rights*
{panel}

* Data is stored locally on device, and users can delete riders
* Recommended: ensure CS has a process for handling data subject requests if a rider contacts us (like we do for Trusted Contacts)

----

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Global rollout* 
{panel}

There are no red flags for global rollout, but I recommend excluding consent markets - i.e. where consent is required for data use. I will ask [~accountid:712020:0b1ccfcb-3809-460a-88ab-c96985ba329a] to chip in on this. We don’t have consent markets in Europe. This means that I am fine with rolling out in Europe, but some International markets might be a blocker

